paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Intended for a host app that drives the SDK in-process and owns its own login","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session, which outlives any one SDK session. Call it on every session change,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including logout, where the correct value is an empty array. An injected empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array means “this user has no teams” and is honoured; it does not fall back to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever a login found.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Shipped on iOS for API parity with Android, where the Analyzer is the caller. No","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in-process iOS host uses it today: everything reaching this SDK arrives through","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Appium, and a fresh session there means a fresh fetch. In ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axeDevToolsXCUI_noauth"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which compiles without analytics, nothing reads this value and no events are sent;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it ships there for API-surface parity only.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entries are dropped rather than sent, and the rest of the array still applies, when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the id is blank, when either field carries control characters, or when either field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exceeds 256 unicode scalars. Past 100 entries the array is truncated. Every drop is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"logged. A blank ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"name"}]},{"text":" is kept: the id is the identity.","type":"text"}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Replaces the team memberships stamped on subsequent events, 